UDP flows of the tun inbound get an idle timer of their own.

An idle TUN flow is closed by the outbound's timer, freedom's userLevel or the
proxy user's level, the same for TCP and UDP; the inbound's level only picks
stats, and the stack's IdleTimeout is set but never read. keqdroid has a UDP
timeout of its own in the TUN settings (sing-box's udp_timeout before the move
to xray). A UDP flow now also ends after connIdle of level userLevel + 1 with
no datagram either way. The outbound's timer still runs, so the flow ends at
the shorter of the two, as it did when sing-box handed UDP to xray over SOCKS.
A level the config does not set has xray's defaults, 300 s, the outbound's
own, so nothing changes until the config sets one.
